            <fr:title text="AI Reasoning Verification: Stepwise Verification via NLI">AI Reasoning Verification: Stepwise Verification via NLI</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Thesis</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="institution">
              <fr:link href="https://www.cam.ac.uk/" type="external">University of Cambridge</fr:link>
            </fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="position">Supervisor: Prof. <fr:link href="/andreasvlachos/" title="Andreas Vlachos" uri="https://mkiyoaki.github.io/andreasvlachos/" display-uri="andreasvlachos" type="local">Andreas Vlachos</fr:link></fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:ul><html:li>Reframed stepwise reasoning verification as local Natural Language Inference (NLI), employing fair comparison of language models with different architectures and training paradigms.</html:li>  
  <html:li>Results showed that discriminative supervision consistently outperforms generative verdict training across both encoder and decoder LMs. (Supported by the Alan Turing Institute).</html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
