            <fr:route>/l101-sft-rl-mechanisms/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Representation vs. Execution: SFT and RL under Distribution Shift">Representation vs. Execution: SFT and RL under Distribution Shift</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Project</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="institution"><fr:link href="https://www.cam.ac.uk/" type="external">University of Cambridge</fr:link> (L101)</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="position">Supervisor: Prof. <fr:link href="/andreasvlachos/" title="Andreas Vlachos" uri="https://mkiyoaki.github.io/andreasvlachos/" display-uri="andreasvlachos" type="local">Andreas Vlachos</fr:link></fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="external">https://github.com/MKiyoaki/l101-project</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:ul><html:li>Investigated post-training dynamics (SFT vs. GRPO) under distributional shifts on Qwen2.5-1.5B using Structural Causal Models and layer-wise linear probing. </html:li>
  <html:li>Demonstrated that outcome-based RL restores syntactic compliance (98.2%) while latent causal rules remain internally encoded (66% probe accuracy) despite generative execution failure.</html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
